  "statement": "ZBP1 was explicitly investigated in the context of PANoptosis in psoriasis but was found to act independently of this keratinocyte death process. SP100 has a very weak genetic association score (0.04) with no mechanistic backing, and AP1G2 only appears as differentially expressed in RNA-seq studies without a demonstrated causal role. The remaining genes (CARS2, KHK, USP6, HELZ2, GUCA1C, IL11, UTP20, IFNW1, MAN2A2) lack functional connectivity to Wnt or interferon signaling networks in this context and have no robust primary literature connecting them to the pathogenesis of psoriasis.",
