   "mechanism": "EIF2AK4 (GCN2) operates as a metabolic stress sensor that phosphorylates eIF2-alpha to attenuate global translation during nutrient deprivation. In epidermal gamma-delta T cells, this kinase restrains the excessive production of the pathogenic cytokine IL-17A. When metabolic stress signals are disrupted (such as during obesity), impaired EIF2AK4 function unleashes IL-17A secretion, severely exacerbating inflammatory psoriasis.",
